ui/node_modules/
npm-debug.log*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Runtime data
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/saves/
data/cache/
data/telemetry/
# Every story builds its own lore index on first run, inside its own tree.
# (The flagship's used to sit at the repo root's data/lore/ until its content
# moved under games/clockwork-dark/data/; this one pattern now covers every
# story, which is the point of them sharing a layout.)
games/*/data/lore/*.db

# Generated media. Session output is disposable; the curated pack that ships
# with the game lives in content/scenes/clockwork/static/art/ and IS committed.
data/media/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Scratch stories — local only
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A sandbox story for testing scenes, characters and agents. It is a real
# installed game (`launcher.py --game dev-story`) and deliberately disposable,
# so it stays off the repository.
#
# Safe to ignore because nothing committed names it. `registry.discover()`
# simply does not find it, `catalog()` returns one fewer row, and no test,
# script or config references the slug. The one thing that WOULD have leaked it
# is a UI plugin directory: Vite turns each `ui/src/stories/<slug>/` into its own
# chunk in the COMMITTED `dist/` tree. It does not need one -- it declares
# `ui: {plugin: wicked-garden}` and borrows an existing skin, which is what that
# manifest key was added for.
#
# The one rule: do NOT put `game.default: dev-story` in `config/default.yaml`.
# That file IS committed, and a fresh checkout would fail activation on a story
# it does not have. `config/local.yaml` is ignored and is the right home.
games/dev-story/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Source design material — local only
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Working documents a story was BUILT FROM, not shipped from. 36.6 MB of
# markdown, mockups and concept plates that the games/ tree has already
# imported, re-encoded and cited by line number.
#
# Ignored rather than committed for three reasons: this repository is public
# and git history is permanent; the concept art here is a second, larger copy
# of pictures that already ship under games/<slug>/data/art/; and these
# documents specify content at intensity tiers the shipped stories
# deliberately stop short of.
#
# The engine never reads it. The suite reads it exactly once -- a test that
# compares the shipped epilogue index to the JSON it was transcribed from --
# and that test SKIPS when this directory is absent, because a provenance check
# with no second document to compare against is not a check. Everything else
# that used to read from here now reads
# `games/wicked-garden/data/canon/state-dictionary.json`, which ships.
#
# Verified by renaming this directory and running the suite: 1314 passed, 1
# skipped. The citations in the content files (`05-BACKSTORY.md:113`) are
# provenance, not a dependency.
Design_files/

